-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock: pure-DBC talent redesigns (no C++ required)
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- Shadowburn (talent 963, all 10 ranks)
--   "Doesn't cost a Soul Shard anymore. Instead generates one, and another if
--    the target dies. Longer cooldown."
--   - Reagent1/ReagentCount1 cleared: no longer costs a shard.
--   - Effect3 = SPELL_EFFECT_CREATE_ITEM (24) granting item 6265 on cast.
--     Spell::EffectCreateItem routes through CanStoreNewItem, which already
--     respects item_template.maxcount = 32, so the cap is automatic.
--   - CategoryRecoveryTime 15000 -> 30000 (the "longer cooldown").
--   - The shard-on-death half needs NO changes: Effect1 already triggers
--     marker aura 29341, which carries SPELL_AURA_CHANNEL_DEATH_ITEM and is
--     gated to XP/honor-worthy kills by the core script spell_warl_shadowburn.
--
-- Destructive Reach (talent 964, ranks 17917/17918)
--   "Threat no longer reduced. Fire damage increased by X%."
--   - Effect2 aura 108 (ADD_PCT_MODIFIER) -> 79 (MOD_DAMAGE_PERCENT_DONE).
--   - MiscValue2 2 (SPELLMOD_THREAT) -> 4 (SPELL_SCHOOL_MASK_FIRE).
--   - BasePoints2 -11/-21 -> 4/9 (i.e. +5% / +10% fire damage).
--   - EffectSpellClassMaskB1/B2/B3 MUST be zeroed: aura 79 with a non-zero
--     SpellClassMask is treated as a restricted modifier and silently
--     applies to nothing.
--     (Column naming: the LETTER is the effect index and the NUMBER is the
--      flag96 word, i.e. B1/B2/B3 are the three mask words of Effect2.
--      DBCStructure.h:1750 lays these out as flag96 EffectSpellClassMask[3].)
--   - Effect1 (spell range, SPELLMOD_RANGE) is left untouched.
--
-- Soul Leech (talent 1678, ranks 30293/30295/30296)
--   "15% chance to return health equal to 200% of the damage caused."
--   - EffectBasePoints1 19 (20%) -> 199 (200%).
--   - ProcChance 10/20/30 -> 5/10/15.
--   The existing core handler spell_warl_soul_leech reads both fields, and
--   the class mask (A1 = 897 / A2 = 192) already covers exactly the intended
--   spell list (Shadow Bolt, Shadowburn, Chaos Bolt, Soul Fire, Incinerate,
--   Searing Pain, Conflagrate), so no mask change is needed.
